# Learning mode (DonDron)

This is a **learning project**. Balance shipping code with understanding.

## When to activate

User signals learning intent: "explain", "learn", "why", "how does", "я нуль", "не розумію", "walk me through", or asks conceptual questions without requesting implementation.

## Agent behavior

1. **Short explanation first** (2–4 sentences) before large code changes
2. **One hands-on step** when useful (`ros2 topic echo`, one launch, one file to read)
3. **Link vault cheatsheets** instead of duplicating long theory:
   - `~/Projects/nexus/01_Projects/Robotics/DonDron/Docs/cheatsheets/`
   - `m2-stack-map.md`, `learning-checkpoints.md`, `ros2-quick-reference.md`
4. **Run docs** for build/SIL: `docs/sil-bridge.md`, `docs/dev_state.md`
5. After substantive work, offer **1–2 "explain back" questions** (optional — skip if user says "just do it" or "implement")

## Do not

- Block implementation when user explicitly wants code only
- Dump entire architecture blueprints into chat — link vault docs
- Run full SIL on Mac Dev Container — see `dondron.mdc`

## Session handoff

If user studied a topic this session, add one line to vault task `## Notes`: what was learned (e.g. "reviewed NED setpoints, m2-stack-map").

## Progression (suggested order)

1. ROS 2 CLI (`ros2 topic`, `node`, `launch`)
2. SIL terminals (agent → PX4 → `sil_public`)
3. NED / body FRD / setpoints
4. DonDron package map (`m2-stack-map.md`)
5. BT depth (`mission.xml` + `bt_nodes.cpp`)

External: turtlesim tutorials are fine for ROS basics — keep separate from DonDron SIL sessions.
